Description: Move touch build-indep-stamp outside nodoc ifeq block
 When nodoc is in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS the entire ifeq block is excluded
 at Makefile parse time, leaving build-indep-stamp with an empty recipe.
 GNU Make then falls through to the %: dh $@ catch-all and calls
 "dh build-indep-stamp" which is not a valid dh sequence (Error 25).
 Moving the touch outside the ifeq gives the rule a non-empty recipe
 unconditionally, preventing the catch-all from firing.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-03
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -61,8 +61,8 @@
 	ln -sf /usr/share/javascript/underscore/underscore.js build/doc/html_subst/_static/underscore.js
 	ln -sf /usr/share/javascript/sphinxdoc/1.0/doctools.js build/doc/html_subst/_static/doctools.js
 	ln -sf /usr/share/javascript/sphinxdoc/1.0/searchtools.js build/doc/html_subst/_static/searchtools.js
-	touch build-indep-stamp
 endif
+	touch build-indep-stamp
 
 clean:
 	dh_testdir
